prompt Keaton: tier 1 and 2 approved, gratitude stays, kg -- inside a much larger grant covering the seed scrub, a scrub template, a Glow-profile molt, contributing and onboarding rewrites, fascia and silo audits, a context-to-foundations question, and a publish.
think This is lap A of eight. Tier 1 and Tier 2 were approved as I wrote them, and what I wrote was Class M mitra shed prep with the cut RED -- so prep is exactly what is authorized, and no file is cut or moved.
think The survey said Tier 1 was five edits. Reading the actual lines made it four, and better. The Grokipedia links in gratitude are attribution and Keaton kept gratitude. The your_model line in personalize.template.brix is a TEMPLATE STUB rather than a mention, so it breaches to a fillable placeholder and serves his later ask in the same stroke.
think And a third trap appeared that the survey missed: the voice_seat_cursor rows in recursion_block.brix sit under a header reading accrete rows; never rewrite a dated stretch, guarded by dated_guard. They stay whatever is cut. Filed on the row so the next hand meets it.
think SHRED_PREP stood at 24,432 of 24,576 with 144 bytes free and two new rows wanting room. A cairn first, then the finished rune-rename cut record folded whole to its own shelf, then the rows.
obs A BANNER ON ITS FACE IS NOT ALWAYS SAFE, AND THE THREE EXCEPTIONS ARE EACH A DIFFERENT REASON. An .arbor file is spoken output, so a banner would be read aloud. A .corpus.bron is parsed. And chatgpt-mind.sh is byte-pinned by its own Rishi peer's header -- editing it falsifies a documented provenance claim even though no guard hashes it. Each carries its banner on the Class M row instead, and the row says which and why.
obs I CHECKED THE BANNERS BY RUNNING WHAT THEY TOUCH RATHER THAN BY READING THEM. Eleven files gained a three-line comment; all three .rish still run, all four shell files pass sh -n, both .awk parse, and arbor_voice and mind_source_adaptation are GREEN. A comment is safe until it is above a shebang, which is why the inserter reads line 1 first.
obs THE ORDER OF THE FOUR TIER-1 EDITS CAME OUT OF READING, NOT PLANNING. My survey listed five sites from a grep. Opening each one turned two into keeps, one into a template improvement, and one into a Class M row. A census names candidates; only reading names verdicts.
